time limit per test: 2 seconds
memory limit per test: 256 megabytes

You are given n elements arranged in a line, numbered 1, 2, ..., n from left to right.
You may delete any number of elements (possibly none). The remaining elements form a subsequence and keep their relative order. Let the length of this subsequence be m. If the element with original index i becomes the j-th element of the subsequence (1 <= j <= m), define
its left rank as j, and
its right rank as m - j + 1.
For each element, you are given two integer segments [li, ri] and [ui, vi]. The i-th element is valid in a subsequence of length m if and only if, when it occupies position j in that subsequence, both of the following hold:
Its left rank is not in the range [li, ri] (i.e., j is not in [li, ri]);
Its right rank is not in the range [ui, vi] (i.e., m - j + 1 is not in [ui, vi]).
A subsequence is valid if every element remaining in it is valid.
Find the maximum possible length of a valid subsequence. The answer may be 0.

Input:
Each test contains multiple test cases. The first line contains the number of test cases t (1 <= t <= 5000). The description of the test cases follows.
The first line of each test case contains a single integer n (1 <= n <= 5000) — the number of elements.
Then n lines follow, the i-th line containing the four integers li, ri, ui, and vi (1 <= i <= n, 1 <= li <= ri <= n, 1 <= ui <= vi <= n).
It is guaranteed that the sum of n over all test cases does not exceed 5000.

Output:
For each test case, print one integer — the maximum possible length of a valid subsequence.

Strategy:
This is 2D dp. We can design the double vector so that dp[i][j] tracks the length of the string at the point where we are trying to get to i chosen elements but we have chosen only j of them so far. This solves the issue with the right rank being dynamic based on the final length m. At the start of the each instance of the inner loop we set and idx=0 which tracks the current element we are trying to assign. Then inside our while loop we check the left and right rank bounds in O(1) and see if the element can be included. If it can we include it and break the loop, if it cannot we go onto the next one. After finishing the double for loop we find the maximum of all dp[i][i] and output that. We cannot do dp[i][j] where i!=j because the state where i!=j is invalid because our whole calculation of the right rank depends on the final length being i which here it is not since we have only allocated j elements.